---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Breadcrumb from '../components/Breadcrumb.astro';
import { breadcrumbLd } from '../lib/seo';
const crumbs = [{ name: 'Home', href: '/' }, { name: 'About', href: '/about/' }];
---
<Base title="About Print & Play Game: free games, real credits" description="What this site is, how we choose games, how licences and hosting work, and how to get in touch or submit a game." path="/about/" jsonLd={[breadcrumbLd(crumbs)]}>
  <Breadcrumb items={crumbs} />
  <section class="wrap" style="max-width:860px; padding-bottom:48px">
    <article class="prose">
      <h1 style="margin-bottom:18px">About</h1>
      <p class="lead" style="margin-bottom:24px">Print &amp; Play Game is a library of free games and puzzles you print at home. Board games, card games, escape games, scavenger hunts, mazes, word searches and bingo cards, plus the rules of the classics.</p>
      <h2>How we choose games</h2>
      <p>We only list games that are free to download and that we have printed and played, or that come from a designer or publisher with a clear licence. Every page credits the designer, the artist and the publisher, and links to the original source.</p>
      <h2 id="licences">Hosting and licences</h2>
      <p>A PDF is hosted on this site only when its licence allows it (Creative Commons, public domain) or when the creator gave us written permission. Otherwise the download button takes you to the creator's own page. The licence is shown on every game page. If you are a rights holder and want something changed or removed, write to us and we will act within 48 hours.</p>
      <h2>Our own puzzles</h2>
      <p>The mazes, word searches, bingo cards and other puzzles made by us are released under Creative Commons BY-NC 4.0: print as many copies as you like at home or in class, share the link, and please do not sell them.</p>
      <h2 id="submit">Submit a game</h2>
      <p>You designed a print-and-play game and want it listed? Send us the PDF or the link, the player count, play time, age and the licence you release it under. We write the page, you keep every right.</p>
      <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
      <p>Email: <a href="mailto:hello@printandplaygame.com">hello@printandplaygame.com</a></p>
    </article>
  </section>
</Base>
